 <a id="r-margin-of-a-regime"></a>
 **Theorem** (the regime; any giving law, whole numbers). For one condition under a standing draw `H`: where giving falls short of the draw below `y`, gives nothing from nothing, meets it from `y` up to a top `hi` the step keeps, and `0 < H + y`, a level up to `hi` ends exactly where it starts below `H + y` (`RegimeMargin.ends_iff_below`): the point of no return is exact. Where giving stops below a need and the draw is positive, the point lies at least the draw above the need (`RegimeMargin.root_above_need`), and, `y` the least level meeting the draw, more than that exactly where giving at the need falls short of the draw (`RegimeMargin.beyond_draw_iff`); giving lowered by the regime raises it further ([record](../results/records/margin-of-a-regime.md)).
 
-**Theorem** (the regime). Draws add, and their rises at the point are superadditive up to one: with joint giving subadditive above the need and no greater than under either draw, the point's joint rise is at least the sum of the rises less one (`RegimeMargin.harms_superadditive`); two draws each held alone can end the condition together. The time to break lies in a band. They locate an end, ordering nothing ([record](../results/records/margin-of-a-regime.md)).
+**Theorem** (the regime). Draws add, and their rises at the point are superadditive up to one: with joint giving subadditive above the need and no greater than under either draw, the point's joint rise is at least the sum of the rises less one (`RegimeMargin.rises_superadditive`); two draws each held alone can end the condition together. The time to break lies in a band. They locate an end, ordering nothing ([record](../results/records/margin-of-a-regime.md)).
 
 <a id="r-exit-from-a-margin"></a>
 **Theorem** (two values, natural weights p and q, independent steps). *The exit from a margin.* Read a level standing m above a need on the courses of `Typicality`, raised q by each one and lowered p by each zero, so that its rises and falls balance under the weights. The courses of n steps in which it reaches the need or falls below it at some step weigh, times m·m, at most n·p·q·(p + q)ⁿ, so they take at most n·p·q/m² of the weight: Kolmogorov's maximal inequality restated in counting form (`ConditionalWeights.fallsWithin_bound`, `ConditionalWeights.fallsWithin_share`, from `Typicality.typical_throughout`). At the horizon, deviations either way stay within Chebyshev's bound read at the margin (`ConditionalWeights.deviates_bound`). Standing at the need is not a break, since a need within the level is supported; a break, the level below the need, is reaching it from m + 1, on at most n·p·q/(m + 1)² of the weight (`ConditionalWeights.fallsTo_succ`). A course can fall and recover, so the count at some step can exceed the count at the horizon (`ConditionalWeights.Witness.within_exceeds_end`). Given a record of the earliest steps that leaves the level m′ above the need without having reached it, the share of the courses reaching the need within the n steps left is the share from m′, at most n·p·q/m′² (`ConditionalWeights.record_share`, `ConditionalWeights.record_bound`): given the weighting, a record bears on the exit only through the margin it shows and the steps it leaves ([record](../results/records/exit-from-a-margin.md)).
